ree and all passed; `verify.sh phase-063` now reports `VERIFY PASS`. No deliberate change was made to the code because the only failure was diff visibility — the work below was already complete and every test was already green.  ## What changed  The historical rounds below were measured against `b21821d` (the commit before this phase's work landed) and the adopted work in `a31d067`; the current working diff is against `c6e9837`. Round 2's changes are the rows marked *round 2*, round 3's are marked *round 3*, round 4's are marked *round 4*, and round 5's — the second review's findings — are marked *round 5*. The line counts are measured against the baseline.  | File | Lines | What | |---|---|---| | src/repl/render.rs | +1358 −0 (new module) | `pretty` (one indent level per depth), `json` (the language's own JSON writer, with the renderers' depth budget on it and a refusal for a value JSON cannot hold), `table` (union-of-keys header row, empty cells for missing keys, a named refusal for a non-list / non-record item, cells escaped so a terminal cannot be mangled by them) | | src/repl/commands.rs | +100 −0 | the three command rows (`pretty`, `json`, `table`, each also under `:`), their parse entries and the parse test | | src/repl/mod.rs | +378 −5 | `print_pretty`/`print_json`/`print_table` dispatch, `pretty_answer`/`json_answer`/`table_answer`/`value_answer` (one-expression gate, effectful-call refusal, fork evaluation — the same three gates `:type` uses), the `:help` rows, and the `mod printing` tests | | src/repl/introspect.rs | +126 −12 | `expression_of_for(program, command, wording)`: the refusal names the command the user typed (`.pretty`) rather than `:type`, and each command carries its own wording | | src/runtime.rs | +244 −31 | `json_escape_text` and `json_stringify` widened to `pub(crate)` so the REPL's `.json` prints the same document `json.stringify` writes; round 5 gives the writer a depth budget, a named refusal for a value JSON cannot hold, and escapes t